MID_LG_Sub_XXX_MessilinaFarm_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_MessilinaFarm_B01_m01_001: Welcome to Messalina Orchards. We sell many\nkinds of produce that are native to the south.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_MessilinaFarm_B01_m01_002: We're famous for our coffee. We even trade it with\nfar-off Fódlan!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_MessilinaFarm_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_MessilinaFarm_B02_m01_001: If you head east along the Saramis Thoroughfare,\nyou'll soon come to Megaira.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_MessilinaFarm_B02_m01_002: They say it's the jewel of the Shield of Dagda, don't\nthey? It's worth a visit—that much I can say.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_MessilinaFarm_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_MessilinaFarm_B03_m01_001: Typically we sell to merchants, but we'll sell to\nindividuals too.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_MessilinaFarm_B03_m01_002: You can find a lot of things here, so be sure to take\na look.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_MessilinaFarm_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_MessilinaFarm_B04_m01_001: We're truly grateful that you helped us rebuild.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_MessilinaFarm_B04_m01_002: My departed husband and I built this place with our\nown hands. It's the beating heart of our family.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_MessilinaFarm_B04_m01_003: There's nobody left to take it on, but...I'll take care of\nit for as long as I can.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_AguinhoVillage_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_AguinhoVillage_B01_m01_001: A visitor? Rare to see travelers make it all the way\nout to this village.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_AguinhoVillage_B01_m01_002: There's nothing particular about this place, but at\nleast you can take your ease before you move on.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_AguinhoVillage_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_AguinhoVillage_B02_m01_001: Wasn't too many years ago that some bandits holed\nup in Lyoshan Fort nearby.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_AguinhoVillage_B02_m01_002: The boss got killed in some kinda dispute. The whole\nband fell apart after that. Gone now.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_AguinhoVillage_B02_m01_003: Still, hope his daughter Sofia's doing fine these days,\nwherever she ended up.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_AguinhoVillage_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_AguinhoVillage_B03_m01_001: Head southeast from here and walk toward the sea.\nBefore long, you'll reach Raivo.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_AguinhoVillage_B03_m01_002: It's a port, so just as you'd expect, there are plenty of\ngoods in the shops, and people from all over.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_AguinhoVillage_B03_m01_003: If you're looking for news, gossip, scuttlebutt, and\nrumor, it's the place to be.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_AguinhoVillage_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_AguinhoVillage_B04_m01_001: North of this village you'll find the Dada plains.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_AguinhoVillage_B04_m01_002: You can find jyoppa growing there, which isn't\ncommon. If you're lucky, you'll be able to pick some.
MID_LG_Sub_KAI_AguinhoVillage_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_KAI_AguinhoVillage_B05_m01_001: A little west of here is Sparrow's Thoroughfare.
MID_LG_Sub_KAI_AguinhoVillage_B05_m01_002: People have caught sight of a splendid\nmeganius there.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_AguinhoVillage_B06_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_AguinhoVillage_B06_m01_001: Things are back to normal around here, and it's all\nthanks to you.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_AguinhoVillage_B06_m01_002: I'd go so far as to say that the whole town's mood\nhas lifted. We won't let petty things hold us back!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OsirisVillage_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OsirisVillage_B01_m01_001: Heh. I knew that strangers would visit this\nvillage today.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OsirisVillage_B01_m01_002: I cast my fortune and that's what it said. So I\nwelcome you to this desert village of Osiris.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OsirisVillage_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OsirisVillage_B02_m01_001: Most of the Nysiades region is covered by the\nChronos Desert.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OsirisVillage_B02_m01_002: It's dangerous! If you get lost, you won't make it\nout alive. There's a beautiful oasis, though...
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OsirisVillage_B02_m01_003: It's full of treasures, tasty treats, and\nlazy aristocrats!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OsirisVillage_B02_m01_004: Well, that's how it was in my dream, anyway. It\nwould be nice if it was true, wouldn't it?
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OsirisVillage_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OsirisVillage_B03_m01_001: The river water isn't fit to drink. It's poisoned by red\nsediment. And as far as I know, it always has been.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OsirisVillage_B03_m01_002: The source of the river is Lake Menor, in the\nmountains up north.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OsirisVillage_B03_m01_003: That's where you'll find the source of\nthe contamination, mark my words.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OsirisVillage_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OsirisVillage_B04_m01_001: I stayed here, hanging onto hope, knowing you would\nsave us. Thank you.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OsirisVillage_B04_m01_002: But that's all I could foresee. The future is an\nunwritten book. We must be the ones to write it.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_CarianeiraPort_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_CarianeiraPort_B01_m01_001: That huge building by the harbor is the famous\namber hall of the Vandahl Trading Company.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_CarianeiraPort_B01_m01_002: Rumor has it the company's big boss was missing\nfor years and just turned up out of the blue.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_CarianeiraPort_B01_m01_003: It's such a huge, impressive company. I want to\nshake the man's hand! 
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_CarianeiraPort_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_CarianeiraPort_B02_m01_001: Heard of Orens? No reason you should have.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_CarianeiraPort_B02_m01_002: It's a small town perched near Bran Narrows.\nYou'll come to it if you follow the coastline northeast.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_CarianeiraPort_B02_m01_003: I grew up there. It's a good place. Lots of\nskilled archers.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_CarianeiraPort_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_CarianeiraPort_B03_m01_001: I don't care how much faith you have in yourself—\nwhatever you do, do NOT go to Nowah's Cave.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_CarianeiraPort_B03_m01_002: There is something terrible hidden there. You can\ntake my word for it.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_CarianeiraPort_B03_m01_003: I can see you're still thinking about going. Don't. Just\ndon't. No matter what. OK?
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_CarianeiraPort_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_CarianeiraPort_B04_m01_001: I appreciate your help, but you can leave the rest to\nus—from Vandahl.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_CarianeiraPort_B04_m01_002: We have emergency funds at the ready. And it's on\nthe orders of the chief executive, so don't worry.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DemonicVillage_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DemonicVillage_B01_m01_001: Stop, you! What's your business with this village,\ntraveler? You have a suspicious look about you.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DemonicVillage_B01_m01_002: I'll let you pass, but know this—I've got my eye\nfirmly fixed on you. So don't try anything.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DemonicVillage_B01_m01_003: As long as you're here, don't forget that it's good\nmanners to spend some coin in the village.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DemonicVillage_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DemonicVillage_B02_m01_001: Ever heard of the Sand-Shadow Fort? It's just a pile\nof old ruins in the southwestern part of the desert.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DemonicVillage_B02_m01_002: I don't know who built it, when, or why...but I smell\ntreasure, don't you?
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DemonicVillage_B02_m01_003: I'm not going to risk my neck for it, though. I'm\nhappy just to get a sniff now and again.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DemonicVillage_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DemonicVillage_B03_m01_001: If you go all the way to the west edge of the desert,\nyou'll find a village called Twalinn.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DemonicVillage_B03_m01_002: I have a friend there, but lately, I haven't heard\na peep.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DemonicVillage_B03_m01_003: We're both old as the hills, so maybe he passed. Sad\nto think of him dying alone out there.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DemonicVillage_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DemonicVillage_B04_m01_001: Our village was saved thanks to you.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DemonicVillage_B04_m01_002: No matter what we've been through, we owe you the\nhospitality, so please—stay and relax!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_PandoraPort_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_PandoraPort_B01_m01_001: Welcome to the Port of Pandora. It's a sophisticated\ntown where you'll find the finest people and goods.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_PandoraPort_B01_m01_002: The shops are well stocked, so I hope you have deep\npockets. You won't be disappointed.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_PandoraPort_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_PandoraPort_B02_m01_001: Since this town is on the Lir Sea, it's become a port\nof call for merchant ships that cross it.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_PandoraPort_B02_m01_002: We even trade with Morfis, the City of Illusion, and\nEnbarr, the Adrestian imperial capital.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_PandoraPort_B02_m01_003: These places are about as cosmopolitan as it gets\noutside of Dagda, but we're far superior.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_PandoraPort_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_PandoraPort_B03_m01_001: On Cape Damasen, which is to the west, you can\nsometimes find yuna mei plants.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_PandoraPort_B03_m01_002: Since the cape is so remote, few people harvest them.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_PandoraPort_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_PandoraPort_B04_m01_001: There's an island. Out there. In the northern sea. Not\non any maps.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_PandoraPort_B04_m01_002: You'll never hear about it. Not from anyone. Nobody\nbut me.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_PandoraPort_B04_m01_003: It's strange. Ominous. Something's wrong with it.\nI feel it.
MID_LG_Sub_KAI_PandoraPort_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_KAI_PandoraPort_B05_m01_001: The other day, I saw a falicorn alight on\nPegasi's Peak.
MID_LG_Sub_KAI_PandoraPort_B05_m01_002: It's true! Nobody here will listen, but I swear it's true!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_PandoraPort_B06_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_PandoraPort_B06_m01_001: I'm grateful that the port is safe, but I don't think I'll\nbe able to launch my boat. The sea's too rough.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_PandoraPort_B06_m01_002: I wonder what conditions are like across the sea.\nPeaceful, I hope.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_TobalinVillage_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_TobalinVillage_B01_m01_001: Welcome, traveler, to the westernmost village in\nall Dagda.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_TobalinVillage_B01_m01_002: There's not much to the village, but we do have our\nspecialties. Did they lure you in, perhaps?
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_TobalinVillage_B01_m01_003: If so, good eye! Buy as much as you like.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_TobalinVillage_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_TobalinVillage_B02_m01_001: Lightstars are incredibly rare plants. 
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_TobalinVillage_B02_m01_002: The good news is that they grow at Smiling Stone,\nwhich is nearby, to the east!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_TobalinVillage_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_TobalinVillage_B04_m01_001: Our village is out here in the middle of nowhere, but\nyou saved it all the same. I cannot thank you enough.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZastaVillage_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZastaVillage_B01_m01_001: We're between the lakes Garamantes and Zorto, so\nwe produce a lot of salt.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZastaVillage_B01_m01_002: There is no shortage of workers coming in, even\nthough this is a pretty small village.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZastaVillage_B01_m01_003: Since there's the salt business, people come and go\nall the time. Merchants too.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZastaVillage_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZastaVillage_B02_m01_001: If you go north from Garamantes Lake you'll find\nan ancient trade route called the Salt Road.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZastaVillage_B02_m01_002: It leads from here to the Aragonian capital, Grand\nAragon, as it's the route salt traders follow.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZastaVillage_B02_m01_003: It's a long, hard road, though. If you take it, be sure\nto seek out the merchant caravans along the way.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZastaVillage_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZastaVillage_B03_m01_001: Entering the desert isn't a decision taken lightly. You\ncould easily die.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZastaVillage_B03_m01_002: Sandstorms don't just make it hard to see—they\nerase your footprints. You could get lost.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZastaVillage_B03_m01_003: Once you start, assume you won't be able to retrace\nyour steps. Don't stray from your path.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZastaVillage_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZastaVillage_B04_m01_001: You saved our settlement? Truly? Thank you!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZastaVillage_B04_m01_002: I thought we were done for! No, really, I thought\nnobody here would survive. So, thank you.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_IoPort_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_IoPort_B01_m01_001: Welcome to Raivo, the port where the trade goods of\nthe Danann Sea glitter and gleam!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_IoPort_B01_m01_002: Things you can't find anywhere else are always\npiled high right here.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_IoPort_B01_m01_003: 'Course, if you want any of 'em, you need cold,\nhard cash.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_IoPort_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_IoPort_B02_m01_001: In the middle of the woodlands to the west you'll find\nLadon Lake.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_IoPort_B02_m01_002: In its depths you can catch a rare fish called a\nDagdandi, or so they say.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_IoPort_B02_m01_003: You're not the first people I've told about 'em.\nThere's been a few anglers on the hunt lately.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_IoPort_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_IoPort_B03_m01_001: Day in, day out, nothing changes. I want some juicy\ngossip! I haven't heard a thing lately.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_IoPort_B03_m01_002: Now Alecto, that's a big city on the ocean. Plenty of\ndirt to be dished, I'm sure. I should move there.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_IoPort_B03_m01_003: It's just to the southwest—and full of traders to boot!\nTons of goods flowing in from faraway lands.
MID_LG_Sub_KAI_IoPort_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_KAI_IoPort_B04_m01_001: Hey, you there! I heard the craziest thing. Why isn't\nanybody listening to me?
MID_LG_Sub_KAI_IoPort_B04_m01_002: There's a monoceros roaming the Oleance plains!
MID_LG_Sub_KAI_IoPort_B04_m01_003: You don't see one of those every day. Exciting,\nisn't it?
MID_LG_Sub_KAI_IoPort_B04_m01_004: Thanks for stopping to listen. If I learn anything else,\nI'll be sure to tell you.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_IoPort_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_IoPort_B05_m01_001: Wait a minute... You can't be the Promised One's\narmy, can you?
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_IoPort_B05_m01_002: So you are... Incredible that you're here in front of\nme right now!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_IoPort_B05_m01_003: I just have to tell everyone about you! Finally they'll\nlisten to me!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BynaOasis_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BynaOasis_B01_m01_001: Oh my, an unfamiliar face. Could you perhaps\nhave come from outside the desert?
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BynaOasis_B01_m01_002: No, your eyes aren't playing tricks on you. Welcome\nto the desert paradise of the Baina Oasis!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BynaOasis_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BynaOasis_B02_m01_001: Somewhere in the desert you'll find Aditi's Cave.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BynaOasis_B02_m01_002: It's named for a foreign mage from long ago.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BynaOasis_B02_m01_003: The stories have it that even though the mage is long\ndead, their secrets are hidden there to this day.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BynaOasis_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BynaOasis_B03_m01_001: West of this oasis is a region called the\nCorpses' Gutter.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BynaOasis_B03_m01_002: Rare torment grass grows there, and if you're lucky\nyou can get your hands on some.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BynaOasis_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BynaOasis_B05_m01_001: I never in my wildest dreams thought this place\nwould be destroyed by the underworld's forces.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BynaOasis_B05_m01_002: We may have lost everything, but at least we have\nabundant water.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BynaOasis_B05_m01_003: If everyone pulls together and shoulders part of the\nburden of rebuilding, it'll be paradise again!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BasqueTown_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BasqueTown_B01_m01_001: Welcome to Barsk Post Town, a great place for\ntravelers to take a break!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BasqueTown_B01_m01_002: Doesn't matter where you're from—we're happy to\nhave you. Well, as long as you can pay your way!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BasqueTown_B01_m01_003: Now buy me a cup of ghosh so we can toast\nyour arrival!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BasqueTown_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BasqueTown_B02_m01_001: Follow the coast north from here and you'll get to\nthe port city of Niiza. Ever been there?
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BasqueTown_B02_m01_002: It's the best—or at least the cheapest—place to\nbuy fish.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BasqueTown_B02_m01_003: Red meat may be tasty, but everyone I know who's\nlived a long life has eaten fish.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BasqueTown_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BasqueTown_B03_m01_001: The area to the east of here, near Kassite, has\nfallen into lawlessness.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BasqueTown_B03_m01_002: It used to be a great place but everything changed\nafter the Cydonia Massacre.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BasqueTown_B03_m01_003: If you need to go there, be careful. It's swarming with\nex-soldiers who are now little better than thugs.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BasqueTown_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BasqueTown_B04_m01_001: Thanks to you, we're saved! Here I thought we'd just\nbe sitting around waiting for the end of the world.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BasqueTown_B04_m01_002: This calls for a celebration. This time, I'll break\nout my personal supply of ghosh and toast you!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_YamanVillage_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_YamanVillage_B01_m01_001: Good to see you, traveler! Surprised you made your\nway all the way out here to Yaaman.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_YamanVillage_B01_m01_002: We're home to a lot of hunters. Abundant game in\nthe countryside.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_YamanVillage_B01_m01_003: In fact, game is about all there is. But make yourself\nat home as best as you can!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_YamanVillage_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_YamanVillage_B02_m01_001: East of here, through the pass, there's a village...\nWhat was it called... Oh, yes, Ribeira.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_YamanVillage_B02_m01_002: I've only been there once. It's not that different from\nhere, so why go?
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_YamanVillage_B02_m01_003: Pretty scenery, though. Did make me a little jealous.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_YamanVillage_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_YamanVillage_B03_m01_001: Go past the Veletta Range Stronghold, and at the\nend of the road, there's a big port city.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_YamanVillage_B03_m01_002: Pandora, I think it's called. You can find some really\nunusual things there.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_YamanVillage_B03_m01_003: They come from all the way across the sea, you see.\nFrom...from...now what's it called...
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_YamanVillage_B03_m01_004: Fódlan. Yes, Fódlan, I think it is.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_YamanVillage_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_YamanVillage_B04_m01_001: Ah, I didn't think I'd make it, but thanks to you\nI have!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_YamanVillage_B04_m01_002: Of course, a lot of places out there still need help.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_YamanVillage_B04_m01_003: I beg you kindly, please save them too.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OrensTown_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OrensTown_B01_m01_001: Oh, my! Are you perhaps a traveler? You must have\ncome far. Welcome to Orens.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OrensTown_B01_m01_002: We don't have much on offer except our\nbaked goods.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OrensTown_B01_m01_003: If you want some to bring back to your friends or\nfamily then, by all means, visit our market.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OrensTown_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OrensTown_B02_m01_001: Hey! Did you see? A huge ship ran aground on the\ncape east of town!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OrensTown_B02_m01_002: My parents don't want me to go, but I want to hunt\nfor treasure. There's treasure, right?
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OrensTown_B02_m01_003: I wish I was a grown-up! Then I could go. Hey! If\nyou go before I do, it's no fair! I told you about it!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OrensTown_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OrensTown_B03_m01_001: A rare plant grows on Mount Aegina.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OrensTown_B03_m01_002: It's called ninokka, and if you're lucky to find some,\nI'd imagine it'd fetch a high price!
MID_LG_Sub_KAI_OrensTown_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_KAI_OrensTown_B04_m01_001: I don't think this is a secret, but it's not something I'd\ntell just anyone, so listen well.
MID_LG_Sub_KAI_OrensTown_B04_m01_002: Northwest of the town, you'll find the Valley of Black\nWings, so named for the black-winged pegasus.
MID_LG_Sub_KAI_OrensTown_B04_m01_003: Now, if you go looking for a black-winged pegasus,\nthat's up to you. Do as you please.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OrensTown_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OrensTown_B05_m01_001: Can't thank you enough for saving this town.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_OrensTown_B05_m01_002: This town means everything to me, so my gratitude\nto you, well, it's as big as can be!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_KiraVillage_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_KiraVillage_B01_m01_001: Welcome, traveler, to the village of Kira.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_KiraVillage_B01_m01_002: I hope you can have a nice rest while you're here.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_KiraVillage_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_KiraVillage_B02_m01_001: A traveler, is it? Come! Come closer!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_KiraVillage_B02_m01_002: Don't you worry... I mean you no harm. I just want\nto get a look at you. Come.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_KiraVillage_B02_m01_003: Yes, you're the spitting image of my dead son.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_KiraVillage_B02_m01_004: Heeheehee!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_KiraVillage_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_KiraVillage_B03_m01_001: Don't...
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_KiraVillage_B03_m01_002: Don't...
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_KiraVillage_B03_m01_003: Don't go near the Masked Woods.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_KiraVillage_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_KiraVillage_B04_m01_001: It's sad, but nobody who's here now originally lived\nin this village.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_KiraVillage_B04_m01_002: We found them all dead, throats cut. It seems they\ntook their own lives when the underworld appeared.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_KiraVillage_B04_m01_003: I can't say what drove them to do it, but perhaps\ntheir concept of death isn't like ours.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_KiraVillage_B04_m01_004: But it's still sad, isn't it? Even if that's true.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZimaPort_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZimaPort_B01_m01_001: Shama may be a port, but we aren't all that used to\nvisitors. Welcome, all the same.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZimaPort_B01_m01_002: Be careful not to travel inland, though. Terrible\nsandstorms make it so you can't see anything.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZimaPort_B01_m01_003: If you venture in, you'll never make it back here.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZimaPort_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZimaPort_B02_m01_001: I hear there's a big tower beyond the desert. Dragon's\nEye Tower, my grandpa calls it.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZimaPort_B02_m01_002: He tells me stories of an ancient hero that hid\ntreasures there. I wonder if they're true...
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZimaPort_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZimaPort_B03_m01_001: I never imagined that help would come all the way\nfrom across the sea.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZimaPort_B03_m01_002: I truly don't know how to thank you for this.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_ZimaPort_B03_m01_003: What's this world coming to, I ask you?
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_WillyVillage_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_WillyVillage_B01_m01_001: This is Whill. Did you get lost? There's no way you\nMEANT to come here, is there?
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_WillyVillage_B01_m01_002: Well, either way, be on your guard. The town is\nplagued by fearsome beasts from the mountain.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_WillyVillage_B01_m01_003: They love the taste of human flesh, so you'd better\nbe ready for them. Heh.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_WillyVillage_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_WillyVillage_B02_m01_001: What's going on here? That mountain is cursed! It's\ncrawling with vicious beasts.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_WillyVillage_B02_m01_002: You look like you're a traveler too, so listen to me—\ndon't even think of climbing it.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_WillyVillage_B02_m01_003: Whatever you do, though, do NOT enter the cave at\nthe foot of the mountain. That's even worse.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_WillyVillage_B02_m01_004: I'm all torn up. Guess I'm stuck here till I heal.\nI don't like it one bit.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_WillyVillage_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_WillyVillage_B03_m01_001: Ah, you're back. Well, things are fine now, believe it\nor not.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_WillyVillage_B03_m01_002: I'm not from around here, and the locals here\nare fearless. I've never seen anything like it.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_WillyVillage_B03_m01_003: They don't back down even when a snarling beast\nstares them in the face. I think they enjoy it!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_WillyVillage_B03_m01_004: Honestly, it's reassuring that they're so tough.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BenetnashVillage_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BenetnashVillage_B01_m01_001: This is Benetnasch! I was born here!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BenetnashVillage_B01_m01_002: There's all kinds of neat stuff around here! I bet you\ncan't guess what's my favorite!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BenetnashVillage_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BenetnashVillage_B02_m01_001: If you look out to the sea north of here, you'll see a\ntiny island. It's called Thiere.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BenetnashVillage_B02_m01_002: Everything I've heard says it's an uninhabited island.\nBut there are some strange plants that grow there.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BenetnashVillage_B02_m01_003: And I've also heard there's something called baquatti\ngrowing there. Apparently it's useful.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BenetnashVillage_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BenetnashVillage_B03_m01_001: Thank you for coming to our rescue. I think we're\ngoing to make it now.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BenetnashVillage_B03_m01_002: Yes, the village is in tatters, but don't worry... We'll\nmake do.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BenetnashVillage_B03_m01_003: Why can't I be stronger? Then I could have\nsaved everyone...
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DimutaineFarm_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DimutaineFarm_B01_m01_001: Welcome to Diamouténé Farm! We welcome\nall travelers.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DimutaineFarm_B01_m01_002: Friends of Halvin, are you? Thank you for looking\nout for her.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DimutaineFarm_B01_m01_003: Feel free to take a look around the shop. We have a\nfew things.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DimutaineFarm_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DimutaineFarm_B02_m01_001: Now that you're here, we're going to be fine.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DimutaineFarm_B02_m01_002: It looks like things are safe for now too. Please, take\na rest here for as long as you like.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_NizaPort_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_NizaPort_B01_m01_001: We of Niiza trade with the Brigid archipelago over\nthe northern sea.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_NizaPort_B01_m01_002: That means you can find things here you can't\nusually find elsewhere.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_NizaPort_B01_m01_003: They say that the people of Brigid craft objects that\nhold the power of spirits. Wonderful, don't you think?
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_NizaPort_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_NizaPort_B02_m01_001: Cross via the Arago route and you'll arrive at a\nfishing village known as Fina.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_NizaPort_B02_m01_002: I wouldn't stop there, though. There are some nasty\nrumors about human sacrifice.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_NizaPort_B02_m01_003: Apparently they're trying to appease the sea. Either\nway, I'd skip the visit.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_NizaPort_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_NizaPort_B03_m01_001: You see that range to the west? That's the Iapetus\nMountains. Everybody knows them.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_NizaPort_B03_m01_002: Legends have it that long ago, bandits used to hide\ntheir treasures in a cave in the foothills.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_NizaPort_B03_m01_003: It's dangerous, though. People who blunder into the\ncave just end up hurt.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_NizaPort_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_NizaPort_B04_m01_001: Thank you. I'll finally be able to launch my ship.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_NizaPort_B04_m01_002: In fact, I'll take this chance to shove off as soon as\npossible. Be seeing you!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_NizaPort_B04_m01_003: Wait, the waters are full of sea beasts? Can't you do\nsomething about THAT?
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DaMina_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DaMina_B01_m01_001: You look lost. This is Da Mina, the town of\nweaponsmiths. You must have heard of it.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DaMina_B01_m01_002: How did you even find us? The town's location is a\nclosely guarded secret.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DaMina_B01_m01_003: If you don't want to die young from inhaling black\nsmoke, you'd best hurry on home.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DaMina_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DaMina_B03_m01_001: If you rode across Lake Menor, then you saw how\npolluted it is.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DaMina_B03_m01_002: It's all due to the town. People just dump their runoff\ninto the lake. They should know better!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DaMina_B03_m01_003: The people of this town are killing the fish just to\nmake weapons—weapons to kill people.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DaMina_B03_m01_004: People have no morals at all. Don't you agree?
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DaMina_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DaMina_B04_m01_001: We lost so much in the fighting. People, our\nbelongings, the town itself...
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_DaMina_B04_m01_002: But even in this sooty wreckage, look...flowers\ncan bloom.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Breston_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Breston_B01_m01_001: Brezarant is a land of bravery and honor, founded by\nthe hero Breza four hundred years ago.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Breston_B01_m01_002: The royal capital, Breston, is its heart!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Breston_B01_m01_003: The city houses an arena, where battles unfold day\nafter day.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Breston_B01_m01_004: Listen and you can hear the cheers of the crowd, the\nclash of metal, and the battle cries of the warriors!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Breston_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Breston_B02_m01_001: Northwest of here, on the other side of Mount Orgus,\nlies the temple to Mars.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Breston_B02_m01_002: If you find you have lost your way as a warrior, it is\ngood to offer a prayer there and hone your heart.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Breston_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Breston_B03_m01_001: To the southwest, at the foot of Mount Orgus, there's\na village called Whill. Take the Warrior's Road.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Breston_B03_m01_002: Why do people want to live all the way out there in\nthe boonies? Aren't they scared of wild animals?
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Breston_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Breston_B04_m01_001: We took inspiration from you and hardened our\ndefenses. If anything else happens, we'll be ready!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Breston_B04_m01_002: We'll hold the line here, so please, worry about the\nneeds of others, till the world knows peace again.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Alecto_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Alecto_B01_m01_001: Alecto is the second biggest city in Saramis, after\nthe royal capital, Megaira.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Alecto_B01_m01_002: Look at that harbor! At all the magnificent merchant\nships moored here!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Alecto_B01_m01_003: They're piled with jewels and delicacies they sailed\nthe world to obtain and bring back here.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Alecto_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Alecto_B02_m01_001: To the east of Alecto is Valhalla Mine. It's huge—you\ncan't miss it.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Alecto_B02_m01_002: Go past it, and you'll get to Lake Brontes.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Alecto_B02_m01_003: Word on the street is, you can catch the rare paradise\nfish in Lake Brontes.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Alecto_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Alecto_B03_m01_001: My grandma works at Messalina Orchards in the\nsouth, you know.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Alecto_B03_m01_002: They sell lots of different produce there. If you like,\nyou should pay it a visit.
MID_LG_Sub_KAI_Alecto_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_KAI_Alecto_B04_m01_001: I was wandering around Axion Gorge not long ago.\nIt's off to the east of town, not far.
MID_LG_Sub_KAI_Alecto_B04_m01_002: While I was there I saw a meganius with pure red\nfeathers. I almost fell over, gobsmacked!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Alecto_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Alecto_B05_m01_001: You really saved our bacon. Soon we'll be able to\nlaunch ships from port again thanks to you.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Alecto_B05_m01_002: Now get going and save everybody else's bacon! And\ncome back here after so we can toast you with ghosh!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Maon_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Maon_B01_m01_001: People love to gossip. "Mahón Castle? That place is\nfull of weirdos!" Hogwash.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Maon_B01_m01_002: Take a look at me. Am I a weirdo? No! I couldn't be\nany more average in looks or personality!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Maon_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Maon_B02_m01_001: Northwest of this town is a strange, ominous place—\nOrion Canyon.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Maon_B02_m01_002: As legend has it, this is where the hero Arago slew\ngiants. The corpses are said to still be there...
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Maon_B02_m01_003: spewing out miasma into the canyon for as long as\nanyone can recall.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Maon_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Maon_B03_m01_001: Ah, you're finally here. I have been awaiting you. My\ndivination foretold your arrival, of course.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Maon_B03_m01_002: On the edge of the desert to the west, you will find\nthe village of Osiris.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Maon_B03_m01_003: I recommend you visit it. That is all. Farewell.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Maon_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Maon_B04_m01_001: We're so grateful to you for restoring the city!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Maon_B04_m01_002: It's said that Mahón Castle is a city of eccentrics,\nand it's true—it really is.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Maon_B04_m01_003: You won't meet people who are so vibrantly\nindividual, fun to be around, or kind anywhere else!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Mons_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Mons_B01_m01_001: Welcome to the fortress city, Mons. Impressive\nwalls, wouldn't you say?
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Mons_B01_m01_002: Prince Helmeric, son of the great king Gladius,\ntransformed this city into a fortress.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Mons_B01_m01_003: Of course, the city is notorious for the Mons Uprising\nthat came about due to the Zodiac Incident.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Mons_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Mons_B02_m01_001: In the heart of the Cougar Woodlands lies the\nCougar Canopy.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Mons_B02_m01_002: Succulent fruit grows there in abundance, and it's\nteeming with forest life.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Mons_B02_m01_003: Paints a lovely picture, doesn't it? It's the first thing I\nsay to any visitor to the city.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Mons_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Mons_B04_m01_001: Things got pretty hairy in the fight against the risen\ndead! I lost count of my close scrapes.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Mons_B04_m01_002: You should have seen me, though. I wasn't scared—\nnot one bit.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Mons_B04_m01_003: Wait, where are you going? We need your protection.\nPlease! I can't take it anymore!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_LegiaTown_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_LegiaTown_B01_m01_001: Regia is a peaceful place. And we keep it that way.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_LegiaTown_B01_m01_002: We have a militia made up of volunteers. Everyone\nkeeps the peace—together.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_LegiaTown_B01_m01_003: Best you don't make trouble while you're here.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_LegiaTown_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_LegiaTown_B02_m01_001: If you head south from this town, you'll come to\nCallianeira at the tip of the cape.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_LegiaTown_B02_m01_002: It's a port town dealing in fine goods from the regions\nringing the Danann Sea.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_LegiaTown_B02_m01_003: In particular, their selection of ghosh is not to be\nmissed. Just thinking about it makes me thirsty.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_LegiaTown_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_LegiaTown_B03_m01_001: You know Sunset Fortress to the east? If you head\nsouth from there, you'll find some odd stones.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_LegiaTown_B03_m01_002: There are three stones there: Farewell Stone,\nStaying Stone, and Resurgence Stone.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_LegiaTown_B03_m01_003: There are cute stories behind the names, you know.\nYou should check them out if you're nearby.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_LegiaTown_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_LegiaTown_B04_m01_001: We're grateful for all you've done, but we can take it\nfrom here.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_LegiaTown_B04_m01_002: The risen dead can't do as they please anymore! The\npeople of Regia won't allow it!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BombaeVillage_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BombaeVillage_B01_m01_001: Welcome to the Hidden Village of Bombae. Only\nthose who are guided here may set foot on this land.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BombaeVillage_B01_m01_002: We who live here preserve the knowledge and \ntechnology of the People of the White Egg.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BombaeVillage_B01_m01_003: O guided one, I will aid you if you so desire. For all\ndisparate fates will soon be gathered to a single path.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BombaeVillage_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BombaeVillage_B02_m01_001: Bombae's secret elixirs are truly wondrous. They are\nalso rare, and few will attain them.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BombaeVillage_B02_m01_002: Every wound, every illness, is fated. The same is true\nof healing.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BombaeVillage_B02_m01_003: If your wounds are healed and you continue your\nfight, then it is surely fate's doing as well.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BombaeVillage_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BombaeVillage_B03_m01_001: I'm sure everybody sounds so formal when they\nspeak to you. Visitors are rare.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BombaeVillage_B03_m01_002: We do have our reasons for staying hidden and\nliving modestly in this place.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BombaeVillage_B03_m01_003: So, please, keep our secret, won't you? I hope that's\nwhat fate guides you to do.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BombaeVillage_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BombaeVillage_B04_m01_001: Tell us that we must continue to resist. Tell us\nour purpose.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_BombaeVillage_B04_m01_002: Tell us that it is not ended—that our fate continues.\nTell us your answer, and it will guide us.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Megaera_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Megaera_B01_m01_001: Megaira, the royal capital of the kingdom of\nSaramis, is an impregnable citadel.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Megaera_B01_m01_002: It easily withstood enemy besiegement during the\nlast war.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Megaera_B01_m01_003: The capital is vital for the defense of Saramis and\nthe entirety of Dagda.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Megaera_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Megaera_B02_m01_001: East of here, beyond Grania Stronghold, you will find\na village called Benetnasch.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Megaera_B02_m01_002: A renowned smith—an artisan—dwells there,\noffering finely crafted weaponry.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Megaera_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Megaera_B03_m01_001: Have you ever been to Valhalla Mine? It's rich\nwith deposits of wootz steel.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Megaera_B03_m01_002: Saramis often crafts its weaponry of wootz steel. It\nis a fine metal for good, sharp weaponry.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Megaera_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Megaera_B05_m01_001: Queen Theodora! Thank goodness you've returned.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Megaera_B05_m01_002: The chancellor is waiting. He needs to see you\nright away!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Megaera_B06_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Megaera_B06_m01_001: I heard Prince Dyan is the one pulling the strings in\nthis Fort Zanbar business.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Megaera_B06_m01_002: I always take rumors with a grain of salt, but I\nwonder if this one's true...
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Megaera_B07_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Megaera_B07_m01_001: Fort Zanbar is a key strategic point in defending\nthis land against Southern Dagda.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Megaera_B07_m01_002: If we don't get it back quick, the situation could\nspiral into something even worse.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Megaera_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Megaera_B04_m01_001: Our strength was insufficient, and we suffered the\nrisen dead to invade our royal capital. You saved us.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Megaera_B04_m01_002: However, we will not fail again. We will defend our\ncapital with our own hands!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_GranAragon_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_GranAragon_B01_m01_001: Welcome to the capital city of the kingdom of\nArago, Grand Aragon.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_GranAragon_B01_m01_002: It is a metropolis etched from the deeds of the\nAragonian people since our land's founding.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_GranAragon_B01_m01_003: Stand in this city and you'll feel as though the very\nweight of history might crush you.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_GranAragon_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_GranAragon_B02_m01_001: Have you been to Mahón Castle to the west? The\ntown there is sizable in its own right.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_GranAragon_B02_m01_002: You can find things for sale there that you can't get\nhere. It makes for an interesting visit.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_GranAragon_B02_m01_003: Bandits roam nearby, though, so be careful if you do\ndecide to go.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_GranAragon_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_GranAragon_B03_m01_001: Hello, traveler. Where are you headed next?
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_GranAragon_B03_m01_002: If your destination lies east, you should pay the Ere\nMountains a visit while you're in the area.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_GranAragon_B03_m01_003: I've heard a rare plant called hingosh grows on\ntheir slopes.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_GranAragon_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_GranAragon_B04_m01_001: The capital is under siege. Will this form part of its\nhistory, or is its history coming to an end?
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_GranAragon_B04_m01_002: The people aren't taking it lying down, though. Bitter\nrivals are resisting cruel fate arm in arm.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_GranAragon_B04_m01_003: History is filled with ugliness. But there are beautiful\neras where people trust and help each other too.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Kassito_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Kassito_B01_m01_001: Thank you. With the Promised One's support, we\ncan hold out hope.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Kassito_B01_m01_002: Even if this town is razed, seeds of hope will be sown\namong the rubble and take root.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_Kassito_B01_m01_003: We will stand tall against the risen dead. Don't think\nwe'll go down without a fight.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_FinaVillage_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_FinaVillage_B01_m01_001: Come on, everybody! Give it your all! Let's bring the\npeace back!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_FinaVillage_B01_m01_002: We won't let Balor take us down without a fight!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_RibeiraVillage_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_RibeiraVillage_B01_m01_001: Thank you. It took all of our effort just to hold\nthem off.
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_RibeiraVillage_B01_m01_002: We'll all be praying for your victory!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_StMeridaBranch_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_StMeridaBranch_B01_m01_001: You're fighting hard and so are we! We'll defend this\nplace to the last!
MID_LG_Sub_XXX_StMeridaBranch_B01_m01_002: We'll put every ounce of strength into our defense.\nWe're counting on you!
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint00_Yes_m01: <TH>
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint00_Yes_m01_001: You have permission to pass. You may proceed.
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint00_Yes_m02: <TH>
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint00_Yes_m02_001: You don't look suspicious. Very well, go on through.
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint00_Yes_m03: <TH>
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint00_Yes_m03_001: I will permit you to pass. Go on.
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint00_Yes_m04: <TH>
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint00_Yes_m04_001: You want to pass through? Sure, why not? Go ahead.
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint00_No_m01: <TH>
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint00_No_m01_001: You look suspicious. Leave, now.
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint00_No_m02: <TH>
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint00_No_m02_001: I can't allow you to pass. Turn back now.
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint00_No_m03: <TH>
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint00_No_m03_001: I cannot allow you to pass. Please withdraw.
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint00_No_m04: <TH>
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint00_No_m04_001: You can't go through. Go back the way you came.
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint01_Yes_m01: <TH>
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint01_Yes_m01_001: You want to pass? I'll allow it, sure.
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint01_Yes_m02: <TH>
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint01_Yes_m02_001: Just give me a moment to search you... Alright, go\non through.
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint01_No_m01: <TH>
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint01_No_m01_001: What makes you think you can pass? Clean up your\nact and try again later.
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint01_No_m02: <TH>
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint01_No_m02_001: I don't like the look of you. Why don't you turn\naround and head home?
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint02_Yes_m01: <TH>
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint02_Yes_m01_001: You may pass, but proceed carefully.
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint02_No_m01: <TH>
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint02_No_m01_001: You need permission to pass, and you don't have it.\nTurn back.
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint03_Yes_m01: <TH>
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint03_Yes_m01_001: Why are you all the way out here? Eh, no matter. Go\non through!
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint03_No_m01: <TH>
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint03_No_m01_001: You say you want to go through? What could you\npossibly be up to? Get back home!
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint04_Yes_m01: <TH>
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint04_Yes_m01_001: Looks like everything's in order here, so on you go.\nA word of warning, though.
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint04_Yes_m01_002: Visibility in the desert is poor due to sandstorms.\nThe paths you take tend to disappear on you.
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint04_No_m01: <TH>
MID_Gmap_CheckPoint04_No_m01_001: What business could you possibly have past here?\nNo one gets through without explicit permission.
MID_Gmap_KAI_Checkpoint00_No_m01: <TH>
MID_Gmap_KAI_Checkpoint00_No_m01_001: Past here is too dangerous for little kids. I can't\nlet you through.
MID_Gmap_KAI_Checkpoint00_No_m01_002: <DLG>Playing Cai's path, you cannot proceed.
MID_Gmap_KAI_Checkpoint01_No_m01: <TH>
MID_Gmap_KAI_Checkpoint01_No_m01_001: What are you doing here, kid? Keep your nose out of\nour business, why don't you? Now get!
MID_Gmap_KAI_Checkpoint02_No_m01: <TH>
MID_Gmap_KAI_Checkpoint02_No_m01_001: I'm sorry, but it's unsafe to proceed. Try again later.